Derived formats

  The When and Do card format derives from published work on implementation
  intentions: Peter M. Gollwitzer, "Implementation intentions: strong effects of
  simple plans", American Psychologist 54(7), 493-503, 1999. The format is used.
  No text from that work is reproduced.

  The five-value confidence vocabulary, the honest run-outcome vocabulary, and
  several operating rules are adapted from the same author's repositories
  AgriciDaniel/secretary, AgriciDaniel/sync and AgriciDaniel/gauntlet-loop-brain,
  and are credited by source in skills/habits/references/methodology.md.

